"""Reviewed duty-level lineage, separate from section enactment credits."""
LINEAGE={
'44-3504/g':{'title':'OMB privacy and security policy','origin':'PRA 1980','date':'1980-12-11','source':'../read/pra1980.html','locator':'§2(a), former 44 USC §3504(f)','text':'The 1980 PRA assigned OMB policies and guidance for safeguarding agency information. The 1995 PRA restated these responsibilities in §3504(g).','events':[('1995-05-22','Restatement','PRA 1995 placed privacy and security oversight in §3504(g).','../read/pra1995.html')]},
'44-3506/g':{'title':'Agency implementation of privacy and security policies','origin':'PRA amendments 1986','date':'1986-10-18','source':'../sources/law/1994-44-35.html','locator':'Former §3506(c)(6), source credit and 1986 amendment note','text':'The 1986 amendments expressly required agencies to implement applicable information policies, including privacy and security of records. The 1995 PRA restated agency privacy and security duties in §3506(g).','events':[('1995-05-22','Restatement','Agency implementation and accountability appear in the current subsection (g).','../read/pra1995.html')]},
'44-3554/b':{'title':'An agency-wide information-security program','origin':'GISRA 2000','date':'2000-10-30','source':'../read/gisra.html','locator':'§1061, former 44 USC §3534(b)','text':'GISRA required an agency-wide program with risk assessments, policies, training, testing, remediation, and incident procedures. The 2002 laws expanded the program provisions; FISMA 2014 retained the program in §3554(b).','events':[('2002-11-25','Revision','The Homeland Security Act revised former §3534. Its general effective date was 60 days after enactment.','../sources/law/pl-107-296.html'),('2002-12-17','Parallel enactment','The E-Government Act enacted §3544; §3549 addressed the parallel subchapter.','../read/fisma2002.html'),('2014-12-18','Replacement','FISMA 2014 replaced the former security subchapters with §§3551–3558.','../read/fisma2014.html')]},
'44-3554/b/5':{'title':'Security-control testing at least annually','origin':'FISMA legislation 2002','date':'2002-11-25','source':'../sources/law/pl-107-296.html','locator':'Title X, §1001, former 44 USC §3534(b)(5)','text':'GISRA already required periodic management testing. The 2002 provisions expressly set a floor of no less than annual testing, with more frequent testing where risk requires it. FISMA 2014 continued that rule.','events':[('2000-10-30','Earlier duty','GISRA required periodic management testing in former §3534(b)(2)(D).','../read/gisra.html'),('2002-11-25','Parallel enactment','The Homeland Security Act enacted the same annual floor in former §3534(b)(5), subject to its later effective date.','../sources/law/pl-107-296.html'),('2014-12-18','Replacement','The annual floor continued in §3554(b)(5).','../read/fisma2014.html')]},
'44-3555/a/1':{'title':'Annual independent security evaluations','origin':'GISRA 2000','date':'2000-10-30','source':'../read/gisra.html','locator':'§1061, former 44 USC §3535(a)(1)','text':'GISRA required an independent evaluation each year. The 2002 laws revised the evaluation requirements; FISMA 2014 continued them under today’s section number.','events':[('2002-11-25','Revision','The Homeland Security Act revised former §3535.','../sources/law/pl-107-296.html'),('2002-12-17','Parallel enactment','The E-Government Act enacted former §3545.','../read/fisma2002.html'),('2014-12-18','Replacement','FISMA 2014 enacted §3555 after repealing both older security subchapters.','../read/fisma2014.html')]},
'44-3555/b/1':{'title':'The IG’s role in the annual evaluation','origin':'GISRA 2000','date':'2000-10-30','source':'../read/gisra.html','locator':'§1061, former 44 USC §3535(b)(1)','text':'GISRA assigned the IG a role in performing or arranging the evaluation, with special rules for sensitive systems. The current auditor language developed through the 2002 and 2014 provisions.','events':[('2002-12-17','Revision','Former §3545(b) specified the IG or an independent external auditor determined by the IG.','../read/fisma2002.html'),('2014-12-18','Replacement','The duty continued in §3555(b).','../read/fisma2014.html'),('2022-12-27','Citation correction','Congress replaced the Inspector General Act citation with Title 5, chapter 4.','../sources/law/pl-117-286.html')]},
'44-3553/b/2':{'title':'Binding operational directives','origin':'FISMA 2014','date':'2014-12-18','source':'../read/fisma2014.html','locator':'§2(a), 44 USC §3553(b)(2)','text':'FISMA 2014 expressly assigned DHS development and oversight of binding operational directives under OMB policy. The surrounding subsections define the covered systems and exceptions.','events':[]},
'44-3553/h':{'title':'Emergency directives','origin':'Cybersecurity Act 2015','date':'2015-12-18','source':'../sources/law/pl-114-113.html','locator':'Division N, Title II, §229(a)','text':'Congress added a separate emergency authority to address a known or reasonably suspected information-security threat, vulnerability, or incident meeting the statutory conditions.','events':[]},
'5-552a/e/10':{'title':'Safeguards for records about individuals','origin':'Privacy Act 1974','date':'1974-12-31','source':'../read/privacy.html','locator':'§3, 5 USC §552a(e)(10)','text':'The Privacy Act requires appropriate administrative, technical, and physical safeguards for records. This duty has its own privacy-law basis alongside later security-program laws.','events':[]},
'44-3607/b/3':{'title':'A-130 definitions in the FedRAMP statute','origin':'FedRAMP Authorization Act 2022','date':'2022-12-23','source':'../read/fedramp-act.html','locator':'§5921(b), 44 USC §3607(b)(3)','text':'Congress expressly adopted A-130’s definitions of authorization to operate and federal information, including successor documents.','events':[]},
'44-3607/b/4':{'title':'NIST’s cloud definition in statute','origin':'FedRAMP Authorization Act 2022','date':'2022-12-23','source':'../read/fedramp-act.html','locator':'§5921(b), 44 USC §3607(b)(4)','text':'Congress adopted the cloud-computing definition from NIST SP 800-145 or its successor. The Special Publication itself was issued in 2011.','events':[]},
'44-3614':{'title':'OMB guidance for statutory FedRAMP','origin':'FedRAMP Authorization Act 2022','date':'2022-12-23','source':'../read/fedramp-act.html','locator':'§5921(b), 44 USC §3614','text':'Congress directed OMB to issue guidance for agency implementation of the statutory FedRAMP program. OMB had established the earlier program through policy in 2011.','events':[('2024-07-25','Implementation','OMB M-24-15 updates FedRAMP policy and implements the statutory framework.','../read/m-24-15.html')]},
}

LINEAGE['5-404']={'title':'IG audits, investigations, and recommendations','origin':'Inspector General Act 1978','date':'1978-10-12','source':'../sources/law/ig1978.pdf','locator':'§4, 92 Stat. 1102','text':'Congress assigned general audit, investigation, and oversight duties to Inspectors General in 1978. The 2022 law restated the IG provisions in Title 5; FISMA supplies the separate annual security-evaluation duty.','events':[('2022-12-27','Recodification','Congress restated the general IG duties in 5 USC §404.','../sources/law/pl-117-286.html')]}
LINEAGE['40-11331/b/2']={'title':'Mandatory minimum information-security standards','origin':'FISMA legislation 2002','date':'2002-11-25','source':'../sources/law/pl-107-296.html','locator':'Title X, §1002, 40 USC §11331(b)(2)','text':'The 2002 legislation required specified minimum information-security standards to be compulsory and binding. Earlier law already provided federal computer-standards authority. FIPS 199 and FIPS 200 implement the categorization and minimum-requirements framework.','events':[('2002-12-17','Parallel enactment','The E-Government Act enacted a parallel standards provision in §304, effective on enactment; the Homeland Security Act had a later general effective date.','../read/fisma2002.html'),('2022-08-09','Amendment','Congress replaced references to the OMB Director with the Secretary of Commerce in §11331.','../sources/law/pl-117-167.html')]}
